:"inference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Element","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type, and spell the type with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shorthand ","type":"text"},{"code":"[count of Element]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let a: InlineArray<3, Int> = [1, 2, 3]","let b: InlineArray<_, Int> = [1, 2, 3]","let c: InlineArray<3, _>   = [1, 2, 3]","let d: InlineArray         = [1, 2, 3]","","let e: [3 of Int]          = [1, 2, 3]","let f: [_ of Int]          = [1, 2, 3]","let g: [3 of _]            = [1, 2, 3]","let h: [_ of _]            = [1, 2, 3]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also use one of the type’s initializers to create a new value.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Accessing-Elements","text":"Accessing Elements","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Just as with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", you can read and modify an element in an ","type":"text"},{"code":"InlineArray","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"using a subscript. Unless you use the memory-unsafe ","type":"text"},{"code":"unchecked","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" subscript,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any index you provide is subject to bounds checking; an invalid index","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"triggers a runtime error in your program.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var values: [3 of Double] = [1, 1.5, 2]","print(values[0])  \/\/ Prints \"1.0\"","values[1] -= 0.25","print(values[1])  \/\/ Prints \"1.25\"","values[3] = 42.0  \/\/ Fatal error: Index out of bounds"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"indices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property to iterate over all elements in order.","type"